# This project is one very large HTML file, so line endings are not a
# cosmetic concern here. If index.html is ever committed with CRLF from
# one machine and LF from another, git sees every one of its ~13,000
# lines as changed: the diff becomes unreadable, and the new blob cannot
# be delta-compressed against the old one, so each commit adds another
# ~700 KB to the pack instead of a few KB. Normalising to LF in the
# repository keeps both the diffs and the pack small.
* text=auto

# Checked out with the endings each tool actually needs.
*.html text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Vendored and minified: one line, no meaningful diff, not our code.
vendor/three.min.js -diff linguist-vendored
